# Docker build context exclusions: keep the image build fast and free of local
# state, build output and scratch work.
#
# `.git` is deliberately **not** excluded. It is 7 MB, and the build reads exactly one thing out of
# it — the commit, the branch and the commit date, which the debug bundle has to be able to name
# (spec 05 §6.2; `Build/Dockerfile` copies the context into a build stage and asks `git` three
# questions). Nothing of it reaches the image: the copy lives in a discarded builder stage, and the
# runtime stage takes two binaries and no more.

.gitignore
docker-compose.yml

# Build output
target
Source/Core/target
Source/WebUI/target
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Local runtime state: checkpoints, notebooks, logs. Never bake a game into an image.
state

# Scratch scripts and captured output used while developing.
ai_scratchspace

# Docs and editor files are not needed inside the image, except the smoke tests,
# the third-party notices (baked beside the assets, spec 08 §5) and the game
# sidecars under Assets/games/ (matched by the Assets/games/*.md copy, not by a bare *.md).
Documents
*.md
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
INFOCompanion.code-workspace
.env
.env.example
